  "landing": {
    "heroTitle": "Protect pumps from cavitation by lifting suction pressure — only when needed.",
    "heroSub": "An interactive, fully synthetic simulation of the GraviGuard concept.",
    "positioning": "GraviGuard targets centrifugal pumps in water networks with variable suction conditions, raising NPSH available dynamically, only when needed.",
    "s1t": "What cavitation is",
    "s1b": "When local pressure falls below vapour pressure, bubbles form and then collapse violently. The collapse pits the impeller, raises vibration and can destroy a pump.",
    "s2t": "NPSHa vs NPSH3",
    "s2b": "NPSH available is what the system gives the pump; NPSH required is what the pump needs. The margin ratio R = NPSHa / NPSH3 tells you how close you are to trouble.",
    "s3t": "Why suction conditions change",
    "s3b": "Tide, strainer fouling, temperature and level all move NPSHa. A fixed margin can be healthy at high tide and critical at low tide.",
    "s4t": "The GraviGuard idea",
    "s4b": "An elevated gravity tank and a modulating valve inject into the suction line when the margin erodes. A check valve on the source line stops the lifted water flowing back.",
    "s5t": "Where it works — and where it does not",
    "s5b": "It fixes NPSH-limited vapour cavitation. It cannot fix recirculation, air ingestion, or fast phenomena outside the valve's response time.",
    "s6t": "See it working",
    "s6b": "Launch the live simulator, run the scenario library, and compare ON vs OFF on a digital twin.",
